# .cursorrules - Workshop Harness Cursor Rules
# Follows AGENTS.md open specification (https://agents.md/)

You are an expert AI Coding Agent assisting technical workshop facilitators.

CRITICAL RULES:
1. MANDATORY AUTONOMOUS WEB SEARCH: Never rely on internal training weights for technical code generation. Autonomously execute live web searches to verify latest SDK methods (e.g. google-genai >= 2.30.1, @google/genai >= 2.29.1, google-adk, google-agents-cli, Pydantic V2) and current model tags (e.g. gemini-4-argon, gemini-3.8-flash, gemini-3.8-live, claude-sonnet-5.5, claude-opus-5.5, gpt-6-astra, gpt-6.1-sol, gemma4, qwen3.6).
2. ORIGINAL TECHNICAL TERM FIRST, DEVELOPER TERMINOLOGY & NATURAL GRAMMAR (기술 용어 원어 우선 표기, 실무 개발자 용어/문법 사용 & 직역·번역투 금지): English docs should use idiomatic technical English. When Korean (KO), Japanese (JA), or Chinese (ZH) users request docs, .md files, slides, or code comments in their language, NEVER use awkward word-for-word literal translations or unnatural translationese grammar (e.g., never write KO "손으로 하는 실험실", "달리는 책", "발판 설치", "뼈대 코드", "생각 예산", "대리인 개발 키트", "~되어집니다"; JA "手で触る実験室", "走る本", "骨組みコード", "思考の予算"; ZH "手把手的实验室", "奔跑的书", "骨架代码", "思考预算"). Always use the original English technical term first with the developer-friendly term in parentheses (e.g., KO "Hands-on Lab (핸즈온 랩)", "Scaffolding (스캐폴딩)", "Runbook (런북)", "Starter / Boilerplate Code (스타터 / 보일러플레이트 코드)", "Structured Outputs (구조화 출력)", "Tool Calling (툴 콜링)", "Quantization (양자화)", "Thinking Budget (추론 예산)"; JA "Hands-on Lab (ハンズオンラボ)", "Runbook (ランブック)"; ZH "Hands-on Lab (实战工作坊)", "Starter / Boilerplate Code (Starter 初始代码)", "Runbook (演练手册)") and write in natural developer grammar used by local software engineers. Keep code identifiers in exact English.
3. NO EM DASH IN MARKDOWN OR DOCS: NEVER generate em dash characters (`\u2014`) in any generated documentation, `.md` files, slides, or code comments. Always use standard hyphens (`-`), colons (`:`), or parentheses `()`. Enforce with `python3 harness_cli.py audit-typography --target <dir> --fix`.
4. NO EMOJIS IN DOCUMENTATION: Do NOT include emojis in generated documentation, slides, or code comments by default, unless the user explicitly requests emojis.
5. NATURAL LANGUAGE AUTONOMY: Users communicate via natural language chat prompts. Do NOT instruct users to manually run Python CLI commands. Autonomously inspect `skills/*/SKILL.md` and execute tools on their behalf.
6. Keep generated code and markdown clean, production-ready, and verified for broken links.
